  "finding": "Arm A (n_active~2125, array ~2.1 MB) shows NO penalty at any v2: -2.2% to +0.8%, overlap everywhere. Arm B (n_active~5245, array ~5.0 MB) separates perfectly at v2=4: v2<=3 gives +12.9..+19.7% (mean +15.2%), v2>=4 gives -2.9..-7.9% (mean -5.4%), a 15.8 pp gap with 0 of 8 misclassified. The sign genuinely flips. So BOTH a large enough array AND v2(stride)<=3 are necessary. The earlier claim that v2=3 is 'milder' is wrong: L=6 (v2=3) is the worst cell measured at +19.7%."
 },
